**Goal** — Persist and safely claim delayed email work and expose a master email switch plus five per-category email toggles.

**Motivation** — Today a notification only reaches a user who opens koda.

**Approach** — Email is off when `SMTP_URL` is unset or blank: nothing is scheduled, the dispatcher does nothing, invites still work and return the link to the admin (D520). Every email path checks `EmailAvailability.configured`. Email category defaults when a user has no `(category, 'email')` row (D517): `ASSIGNED`, `MENTIONED`, `FLEET_NEEDS_YOU` on; `WATCHED_ACTIVITY`, `FLEET_HEALTH` off. The in-app default stays "missing row = on". Define `EMAIL_CATEGORY_DEFAULTS` in `apps/api/src/notifications/notification.types.ts` alongside the existing category constants. The email master switch is the package's `NotificationPreference` row `(userId, KODA_TENANT_ID, 'email')`; a missing row means on. Email requires both the master switch and the category toggle on. Retries: `EMAIL_MAX_ATTEMPTS` (default 5); backoff `2^(attempts-1)` minutes; claim lock 2 minutes; batch 20; tick every 30 000 ms. `EmailScheduleRepository.claimDue(now, limit)` is one SQL statement: `UPDATE "EmailSchedule" SET status='SENDING', "lockedUntil"=now+2min, attempts=attempts+1 WHERE id IN (SELECT id ... WHERE kind IN ('NOTIFICATION','MEMBER_ADDED') AND ((status='PENDING' AND "dueAt"<=now) OR (status='SENDING' AND "lockedUntil"<now)) ORDER BY "dueAt" LIMIT limit FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED) RETURNING ...` — the same SKIP LOCKED pattern as `apps/api/src/outbox/prisma-outbox.store.ts`. `INVITE` rows are never claimed. Every caller goes through `EmailScheduleService`. Schema `EmailSchedule`: id cuid primary key; kind, unique nullable notificationId with onDelete Cascade to Notification, inviteId, userId, projectId, toEmail, locale default en, status default PENDING, skipReason, attempts default 0, dueAt, lockedUntil, lastError capped at 500, sentAt, createdAt, updatedAt; index `(status,dueAt)`. Migration `20261010100000_email_schedule` must have no semicolon within a statement and zero schema drift. Provide repository privately and service globally via EmailCoreModule. PUT updates only supplied master/item fields; GET includes availability. Regenerate `openapi.json` after DTO change.

**Interface**
```typescript
type PreferencesView = { emailAvailable: boolean; emailEnabled: boolean; items: { category: NotificationCategory; inApp: boolean; email: boolean }[] };
list(userId: string): Promise<PreferencesView>;
update(userId: string, change: { emailEnabled?: boolean; items?: { category: NotificationCategory; inApp?: boolean; email?: boolean }[] }): Promise<void>;
emailAllowedUserIds(userIds: readonly string[], category: NotificationCategory): Promise<ReadonlySet<string>>;
emailAllowed(userId: string, category: NotificationCategory): Promise<{ allowed: true } | { allowed: false; reason: 'EMAIL_OFF' | 'CATEGORY_OFF' }>;
scheduleNotifications(rows: ReadonlyArray<{ notificationId: string; userId: string; toEmail: string; dueAt: Date }>): Promise<number>;
scheduleMemberAdded(input: { userId: string; projectId: string; toEmail: string; locale: string; dueAt: Date }): Promise<void>;
startInviteSend(input: { inviteId: string; toEmail: string; locale: string; now: Date }): Promise<EmailScheduleRow>;
claimDue(now: Date, limit: number): Promise<EmailScheduleRow[]>;
closeAbandonedInvites(now: Date): Promise<number>;
markSent(id: string, now: Date): Promise<void>; markSkipped(id: string, reason: SkipReason): Promise<void>; markFailed(id: string, error: string): Promise<void>; retryAt(id: string, dueAt: Date, error: string): Promise<void>;
type EmailScheduleRow = { id: string; kind: EmailKind; notificationId: string | null; inviteId: string | null; userId: string | null; projectId: string | null; toEmail: string; locale: string; attempts: number; dueAt: Date };
```

**Scope** — In: schema/migration, claim/state service, preference DTO/controller/service, global providers and existing DI/unit assertions. Out: writer scheduling/dispatcher (US-002), web controls (US-003), invite entity (US-004).

**Goal** — Atomically schedule opted-in new in-app notifications and deliver only still-unread emails through a nonoverlapping retrying dispatcher.

**Motivation** — Today a notification only reaches a user who opens koda.

**Approach** — Delayed send (D518): a notification email is due `EMAIL_DELAY_SEC` (default 300) after the notification's `createdAt`, or `EMAIL_APPROVAL_DELAY_SEC` (default 60) when `Notification.kind === 'approval_requested'`, and is sent only if the notification is still unread at send time. One email per notification (D519). `NotificationWriter.deliver(drafts)`: same steps, plus one `EmailSchedule` row per inserted notification whose user allows email for its category (only when `EmailAvailability.configured`), scheduled through `EmailScheduleService.scheduleNotifications`. The `insertMany` call and the scheduling call run inside one `txManager.run`, so a scheduling failure rolls back the inserted notifications and the outbox retry redoes both; the `UserEventBus` publishes run after that transaction commits. Constructor gains `EmailScheduleService`, `EmailAvailability`, `NotificationEmailRecipients` and `TRANSACTION_MANAGER`. `NotificationsRepository.insertMany(drafts)` returns `{ id, userId, category, kind, createdAt }[]`. `EmailDispatcher.tick(now)` first closes abandoned invite sends, then claims, then per row: `EmailContentBuilder.build(row)` returns either `{ skip: SkipReason }` or `{ data, userId }`; a skip marks the row `SKIPPED`; otherwise `sendOne` calls `NOTIFY_SERVICE.send` with `tenantId: KODA_TENANT_ID`, `channel: 'email'`, `templateCode: row.kind`, `locale: row.locale`, `recipient: row.toEmail`. One row's error never stops the batch. A scheduled tick runs about every 30 seconds and does not overlap a running tick. Build order for a NOTIFICATION row (US-002): notification missing → `SOURCE_GONE`; `readAt` set → `READ`; user missing or disabled → `USER_DISABLED`; `emailAllowed` not allowed → its reason; otherwise data `{ title, body: body ?? '', url: webUrl(link), prefsUrl: webUrl('/settings/notifications') }`. SMTP or transport failure on a scheduled row → row back to `PENDING` with `dueAt = now + 2^(attempts-1)` minutes and `lastError` (first 500 characters); after `EMAIL_MAX_ATTEMPTS` → `FAILED`. `PermanentNotificationError`, or `NotifyException` with code `TEMPLATE_NOT_FOUND`, `CHANNEL_NOT_REGISTERED` or `TENANT_MISMATCH` → `FAILED` on the first attempt. A `FAILED` row logs one WARN with the row id, kind and attempts only — never the address, the body or the URL. A builder or repository error for one claimed row → that row returns to `PENDING` with backoff; the rest of the batch continues. `MEMBER_ADDED` and `INVITE` email are transactional notices: they do not consult notification preferences or the email master switch. Extend NotificationsModule providers/exports; stub NOTIFY_SERVICE for DI tests.

**Interface**
```typescript
class NotificationEmailRecipients { emails(userIds: readonly string[]): Promise<ReadonlyMap<string, string>>; }
class EmailContentBuilder { build(row: EmailScheduleRow): Promise<{ skip: SkipReason } | { data: Record<string, unknown>; userId: string | null }>; }
class EmailDispatcher { tick(now: Date): Promise<void>; sendOne(row: EmailScheduleRow, templateCode: string, data: Record<string, unknown>, userId: string | null, now: Date, retryable?: boolean): Promise<'SENT' | 'FAILED' | 'RETRY'>; }
```

**Scope** — In: new-notification schedule, English content, channel sending, retries and idempotent outbox-to-send integration. Out: MEMBER_ADDED builder branch and inline invite mail (US-004), backfilling old notifications, agent recipients, digests, batching and BullMQ/Redis/notify queue processing.

**Goal** — Let a project admin add an existing active user directly or invite a new address with a one-time link and optional inline email.

**Motivation** — Adding a person to a project currently requires a global admin to create an account and hand over a password.

**Approach** — Invite token: 32 random bytes, base64url (43 characters); stored only as its sha256 hex; expires after `INVITE_TTL_DAYS` (default 7). `ProjectInvite` fields: id cuid, projectId (cascade project), normalized email, role ADMIN|DEVELOPER|VIEWER, unique tokenHash, status default PENDING (PENDING|ACCEPTED|EXPIRED|CANCELLED), invitedById (cascade user), acceptedByUserId, acceptedAt, expiresAt, createdAt, updatedAt; index `(projectId,email,status)`. Migration `20261010110000_project_invites` must contain no internal semicolons and have zero drift. Invite create (US-004) order: resolve project → `assertProjectAdmin` → normalise email (trim, lowercase) → `findUserIdByEmail`. Existing active user: create membership (unique violation → 409), schedule `MEMBER_ADDED` due now when configured, return `{ outcome: 'ADDED', member }`. Existing disabled user → 409. No user: in one transaction cancel any PENDING invite for `(projectId, email)` and create a new one; after commit, when configured, send the `INVITE` email inline (`InviteMailer`); return `{ outcome: 'INVITED', invite, invitePath: '/invite/' + raw, emailed }`. Inline invite mail (US-004): `InviteMailer.sendInvite` records an `INVITE` `EmailSchedule` row (status `SENDING`, attempts 1, lock now+2min) and sends it once through the dispatcher's send step with retry disabled, with data `{ projectName, inviterName, role, url: webUrl('/invite/' + raw), expiresAt }`; a successful send → `emailed: true`; anything else, including a thrown error, → `emailed: false` and the row `FAILED`. Invite email locale is `zh` when the create or resend request's `Accept-Language` starts with `zh`, otherwise `en`. `MEMBER_ADDED` and notification email are always `en`. Build order for a MEMBER_ADDED row (US-004): user missing or disabled → `USER_DISABLED`; project missing or soft-deleted → `SOURCE_GONE`; membership missing → `SOURCE_GONE`; otherwise `{ projectName, role, url: webUrl('/' + slug) }`. `MEMBER_ADDED` and `INVITE` email are transactional notices: they do not consult notification preferences or the email master switch. `ProjectInvitesModule` imports `NotificationsModule` for `EmailDispatcher`, and `ProjectMembersModule`'s service is not imported: the invites repository owns its own membership and user writes. Register `ProjectInvitesModule` in `apps/api/src/app.module.ts`. `ProjectInvitesController` create and list return Swagger DTOs; GET lists newest first with effective EXPIRED for overdue pending invites, never a token/hash; use localized error keys in en/zh. Regenerate openapi.json.

**Interface**
```typescript
function generateInviteToken(): { raw: string; hash: string };
function hashInviteToken(raw: string): string;
function effectiveStatus(record: ProjectInviteRecord, now: Date): InviteStatus;
class ProjectInvitesService { create(slug: string, input: CreateInviteDto, principal: KodaPrincipal, locale: string): Promise<InviteCreateResultDto>; list(slug: string, principal: KodaPrincipal): Promise<InviteDto[]>; }
class InviteMailer { sendInvite(input: { inviteId: string; toEmail: string; locale: string; rawToken: string; projectName: string; inviterName: string; role: string; expiresAt: Date }): Promise<boolean>; }
class InviteCreateResultDto { outcome: 'ADDED' | 'INVITED'; member?: ProjectMemberDto; invite?: InviteDto; invitePath?: string; emailed?: boolean; }
type InviteDto = { id: string; email: string; role: string; status: InviteStatus; inviterName: string; expiresAt: Date; createdAt: Date };
```

**Scope** — In: model/admin create-list, role guard, existing-user membership, invitation creation, immediate mail, MEMBER_ADDED content. Out: resend/cancel/public preview/accept (US-005), CLI (US-006), web panel (US-007), storing raw token or retrying invite mail.

**Goal** — Complete single-use invite redemption, token rotation and cancellation, with sessions issued for newly created members.

**Motivation** — A project admin needs to onboard someone without handing over a password, even when registration is closed.

**Approach** — Accept (US-005) is one transaction: a conditional update flips the invite `PENDING → ACCEPTED` only when the hash matches and `expiresAt > now` (zero rows → 404); if a user with the invite email exists (case-insensitive match) → 409 and the transaction rolls back; a unique violation on the user's email (a concurrent accept of another invite for the same address) is also a 409; otherwise create the user (password hashed as `UsersAdminService.create` does, role `MEMBER`, email from the invite, name from the body), set `acceptedByUserId`, create the membership. The session is issued after commit through `AuthService.issueSession`; import `AuthModule` (which exports AuthService) into `ProjectInvitesModule` when adding `InviteAcceptanceService`. `GET /invites/:token` is public, throttled, and returns `{ projectName, projectSlug, email, role, inviterName, expiresAt }`; unknown/expired/cancelled/accepted tokens produce identical 404 responses. `POST /invites/:token/accept` takes name and password validated like RegisterDto and returns login-shaped session at 201; @Public and the same AUTH_LOGIN_LIMIT throttle (5/60s default and env override) as register. Resend by project ADMIN/global ADMIN rotates tokenHash, resets PENDING and expiresAt to now + INVITE_TTL_DAYS, returns new invitePath and emailed, and accepts only PENDING or expired invites; cancel changes PENDING to CANCELLED and leaves final records unchanged. Unknown or wrong-project invite ids → 404; accepted resend → 409. Move the class-load constant from auth.controller.ts to auth-throttle.ts. Refactor register, login and refresh to issueSession as well; preserve disabled/revoked checks. Regenerate openapi.json for resend, cancel, preview and accept DTOs. All integration tests boot with REGISTRATION_ENABLED false; clear DefaultThrottlerGuard in-memory storage between requests as in admin-users.integration.spec.ts.

**Interface**
```typescript
class AuthService { issueSession(user: UserDomain): { accessToken: string; refreshToken: string; user: UserResponseDto }; }
export const AUTH_LOGIN_LIMIT: number;
class ProjectInvitesService { resend(slug: string, id: string, principal: KodaPrincipal, locale: string): Promise<{ invite: InviteDto; invitePath: string; emailed: boolean }>; cancel(slug: string, id: string, principal: KodaPrincipal): Promise<void>; }
class InviteAcceptanceService { preview(token: string): Promise<InvitePreviewDto>; accept(token: string, body: AcceptInviteDto): Promise<{ accessToken: string; refreshToken: string; user: UserResponseDto }>; }
```

**Scope** — In: public preview/accept, admin resend/cancel, password validation, guarded session issuing. Out: admin create/list (US-004), CLI (US-006), Nitro/web accept UI (US-007), password reset and custom lockout.

**Goal** — Provide project-admin terminal commands to invite, list, resend and cancel through the generated API client.

**Motivation** — A project admin needs to bring a new person into a project without a global admin handing over a password.

**Approach** — `koda member invite --email <e> --role <ADMIN|DEVELOPER|VIEWER> [--project <slug>] [--json]`; `koda member invites [--project <slug>] [--cancel <id>] [--resend <id>] [--json]`. stdout: human lines below, or `JSON.stringify(data, null, 2)` with `--json`; stderr: errors through `handleApiError`. Exit codes come from `handleApiError`: 0 success; 1 an API 409 or a network error; 2 config/auth error (401/403); 3 validation error (400); 4 not found (404). Human output: `Added <email> as <role>`; `Invite created for <email>. Emailed.`; `Invite created for <email>. Share this link (shown once): <invitePath>`; `invites` prints a table with headers `ID`, `Email`, `Role`, `Status`, `Expires`. Resend prints its new invitePath. Run `bun run generate` from the monorepo root after API routes/DTOs are complete; do not hand-edit generated code. Call `projectInvitesControllerCreate`, `projectInvitesControllerList`, `projectInvitesControllerResend`, `projectInvitesControllerCancel` via withContext/unwrap/handleApiError; preserve existing member commands.

**Interface**
```typescript
projectInvitesControllerCreate({ path: { slug }, body: { email, role } });
projectInvitesControllerList({ path: { slug } });
projectInvitesControllerResend({ path: { slug, id } });
projectInvitesControllerCancel({ path: { slug, id } });
```

**Scope** — In: member command group and generated client regeneration. Out: API invite routes (US-004/005) and web invite UI (US-007).

**Goal** — Let project admins create/manage invites and let guests redeem a link into a cookie-backed session and project membership.

**Motivation** — A project admin needs to onboard a new person without handing over a password, including when SMTP is unavailable.

**Approach** — Web accept page (US-007) uses the vee-validate + zod form pattern of `apps/web/pages/register.vue`. Web accept (US-007) goes through a Nitro route `apps/web/server/api/invites/[token]/accept.post.ts` that sets the httpOnly auth cookies exactly like `apps/web/server/api/auth/register.post.ts`. Web `useAuth()` — `apps/web/composables/useAuth.ts`: Baseline: `{ user, isAuthenticated, login, register, logout, fetchUser, refresh }`. Target: adds `acceptInvite(token: string, body: { name: string; password: string }): Promise<void>`, which posts `body` to `/api/invites/<token>/accept` (the Nitro route) and sets `user` from the response, like `register`. Web route middleware — `apps/web/middleware/auth.global.ts`: a path starting with `/invite/` returns before the unauthenticated redirect. `ProjectInvitesPanel` sits beside `ProjectMembersPanel` on project settings, opens an invite dialog, loads the pending list and issues create/resend/cancel through `useProjectInvites(slug)`, emits member-added for ADDED so the settings page refreshes its member list, and shows an absolute one-time share link using window.location.origin when INVITED or resent. Confirm cancel. Preview via useApi GET on public page, show signed-in state instead of accept form when authenticated, navigate to /<projectSlug> on success, show invalid and account-exists localized text on respective 404/409. Use interpolated text, not HTML, for untrusted invite display. Update both locale JSON files and cover Nitro cookie forwarding.

**Interface**
```typescript
useProjectInvites(slug: string): { invites: Ref<InviteDto[]>; load(): Promise<void>; create(email: string, role: 'ADMIN' | 'DEVELOPER' | 'VIEWER'): Promise<InviteCreateResultDto>; resend(id: string): Promise<{ invitePath: string; emailed: boolean }>; cancel(id: string): Promise<void> };
inviteLink(path: string): string;
useAuth().acceptInvite(token: string, body: { name: string; password: string }): Promise<void>;
```

**Scope** — In: project invite panel, public accept screen, public-route exemption, Nitro httpOnly cookies, locale and UI tests. Out: API invitation business rules (US-004/005), CLI commands (US-006), Playwright invite end-to-end test.
